      "text": "To determine how far Jana will walk in 10 minutes, we start by finding her walking rate in miles per minute. We know that it takes her 24 minutes to walk one mile. Therefore, her walking rate is:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Walking rate} = \\frac{1 \\text{ mile}}{24 \\text{ minutes}}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find out how far she will walk in 10 minutes. We do this by multiplying her walking rate by the number of minutes she is walking:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Distance walked in 10 minutes} = \\left( \\frac{1 \\text{ mile}}{24 \\text{ minutes}} \\right) \\times 10 \\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the expression, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Distance walked in 10 minutes} = \\frac{10}{24} \\text{ miles}\n\\]\n\nTo convert this fraction to a decimal, we perform the division:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{10}{24} \\approx 0.416667\n\\]\n\nRounding this to the nearest tenth, we get:\n\n\\[\n0.416667 \\approx 0.4\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the distance Jana will walk in 10 minutes is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{0.4}\n\\]",
